# TUI-DESIGN-4 §2.5 / §10 S6 (`narrow.steps`): the narrow ladder under a fault-free session. At 12×40 the console
# is flat, the wordmark is gone and every row must still fit the terminal — which is what the §11 rows
# `no frame taller than the terminal` and V22 (every box row exactly the rule-row width) are checked against
# here. The draft is long enough to exercise the composer's own truncation at the narrowest tier.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.6
send a fairly long draft that cannot fit on one narrow row at all
sleep 0.5
send \x03
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
